# Claude Code Docker Configuration
# Copy this file to claude-docker.conf and edit to match your setup.

# ── Workspace ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default directory to mount as /workspace in the container.
# If unset, defaults to $PWD (wherever you run the script from).
# Can always be overridden per-session:
#   ./run-claude.sh my-project --work-dir ~/other/repo
# WORKSPACE_DIR="/path/to/your/project"

# ── Authentication ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# How to provide Claude Code credentials. Pick ONE method:
#
# Method 1: macOS Keychain (default if on macOS)
#   Claude Code stores OAuth creds in Keychain after 'claude' login.
#   Set your macOS username here.
AUTH_METHOD="keychain"
KEYCHAIN_ACCOUNT="your-macos-username"
#
# Method 2: Credentials file
#   Point to an existing .credentials.json file on disk.
#   (e.g. ~/.claude/.credentials.json on Linux after logging in)
# AUTH_METHOD="file"
# CREDENTIALS_FILE="$HOME/.claude/.credentials.json"
#
# Method 3: API key
#   Use an Anthropic API key instead of OAuth.
# AUTH_METHOD="api-key"
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."

# ── SSH for Git ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How Claude Code authenticates with GitHub/GitLab for git push/pull.
# Pick ONE method:
#
# Method 1: SSH key file (default)
#   Path to your private key ON THE HOST. It will be mounted read-only.
SSH_METHOD="key-file"
SSH_KEY_PATH="$HOME/.ssh/id_ed25519"
#
# Method 2: SSH agent forwarding
#   Forwards your running ssh-agent into the container.
#   Make sure ssh-agent is running and your key is added (ssh-add -l).
# SSH_METHOD="agent"
#
# Method 3: No SSH
#   Use HTTPS for git instead. Claude won't be able to push over SSH.
# SSH_METHOD="none"

# ── Plugins ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Plugins live in a per-container Docker volume (claude-plugins-linux),
# isolated from the host's ~/.claude/plugins so Linux-native binaries and
# container-relative installPaths don't collide with the host's. The volume
# starts empty, so define the plugin set here; the entrypoint installs it on
# startup. Idempotent — already-installed plugins are skipped, so this only
# does real work on the first run (or when you add an entry).
#
# SOURCE RULE: only GitHub marketplaces are officially supported, because the
# firewall (init-firewall.sh) allowlists GitHub by default. To use any other
# source (GitLab, a private host, a raw URL), you must add its domains to
# EXTRA_ALLOWED_DOMAINS below AND adjust init-firewall.sh accordingly —
# otherwise the install will hang/fail on a blocked connection.
#
# PLUGIN_MARKETPLACES: space-separated GitHub repos (owner/repo) to register.
# PLUGINS: space-separated <plugin>@<marketplace> entries to install. The
#   <marketplace> is the marketplace's declared name (e.g. anthropics/
#   claude-plugins-official declares the name "claude-plugins-official").
# PLUGIN_MARKETPLACES="anthropics/claude-plugins-official"
# PLUGINS="superpowers@claude-plugins-official skill-creator@claude-plugins-official"

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Extra domains to allowlist in the firewall (space-separated).
# GitHub and Anthropic services are always allowed.
# EXTRA_ALLOWED_DOMAINS="gitlab.com bitbucket.org"

# Docker image name (change if you run multiple configs)
# IMAGE_NAME="claude-code"
